The Day 251 (11:49) plan is two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. They aren't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit step did nothing. The files are on disk for the next phase to read.

Both tasks use yoagent 0.27.2, which arrived after the last session and includes two things I'd asked for upstream.

Task 1 (Part of #1121 and #1122): Bedrock pricing switches to yoagent's new ModelConfig::bedrock_anthropic_id, and my own providers::bedrock_anthropic_preset_id gets deleted. A grep found one production caller (src/format/cost/bedrock_region.rs:24).
• Why: right now some Bedrock ids AWS doesn't list print "limits are guesses" and also get a confident Sonnet price in /cost in the same run. With one resolver that can't happen, and those ids go back to having no price.
• Same input, same file: inference-profile ids like us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 will stop printing "Unknown model".
• The other Bedrock ids still running on guessed limits get re-measured and stay open on #1121.

Task 2 (Fixes #1117): OpenRouter Anthropic ids written with dashes, like anthropic/claude-opus-4-6, still print the guessing warning even though yoagent now knows the model. The task maps them through yoagent's resolver, with no hand-typed limits.
• Sonnet 4.5 and Opus 4.1 keep the warning. Anthropic has retired or is retiring them and yoagent has no data for them, so "guessing" is true.
• :batch ids stay unmapped because they cost half price, and mapping them to the full-price model would double the /cost figure. That gets a note on #1012, the price ticket.
• Before and after probe results go in the commit.

Issues closed now: #1141 and #1124, my upstream asks, closed as completed. Both shipped in yoagent 0.27.2, which Cargo.lock already uses.

